<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mieszko IV Tanglefoot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1211</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Mieszko I Tanglefoot</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mieszko IV Tanglefoot was a Piast duke of Silesia, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-ii-the-exile">Władysław II the Exile</a>. In 1172 he received a duchy around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raciborz">Racibórz</a>, and in 1202 he added <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opole">Opole</a>, creating the Duchy of Opole and Racibórz, the core of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-silesia">Upper Silesia</a>. In 1210 he briefly seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> and the title of high duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, shortly before his death in 1211.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mieszko-iv-tanglefoot.jpg" alt="Mieszko IV Tanglefoot" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mieszko_IV.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
